docs\journeys\scratch\actor-vs-building-render-diff.md:12:- Keep the sprite-hide suppression disabled until visibility is confirmed, since the current diagnostic comments already leave `rd.has_normal_render[i]` untouched.
docs\journeys\scratch\all-phases-on-audit.md:7:- `Mod.Init()` wires the runtime drivers in a fixed startup order, but the actual frame work is split across multiple Unity `Update`/`LateUpdate` components: `VoxelFrameDriver`, `WorldUIRenderer`, `RuntimeStatsOverlay`, `TimeOfDay`, and `ProceduralSky` ([Mod.cs:38-82](../../../WorldSphereMod/Code/Mod.cs#L38-L82)). The main sink is `VoxelFrameDriver.LateUpdate()`, which flushes meshes, updates water, sun, decals, and post-FX in one pass ([VoxelRender.cs:548-599](../../../WorldSphereMod/Code/Voxel/VoxelRender.cs#L548-L599)).
docs\SETTINGS-AUDIT.md:60:| `ProfilerDump` | Debug | Shows the runtime performance overlay. | `EnableProfilerOverlay` | rename |
docs\journeys\scratch\camera-resolution-audit.md:11:4. The two-camera interaction is the important visibility risk. `MeshInstanceBatcher.ResolveRenderCamera()` prefers the enabled `CameraManager.MainCamera`, otherwise it falls back to `Camera.main` (`MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:288`, `MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:290`, `MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:292`, `MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:295`); `ResolveRenderLayer()` then derives the layer from whichever camera won that race (`MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:298`, `MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:300`, `MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:305`). In a WorldBox scene with a gameplay camera plus `EffectsCamera`, that means the render path is still sensitive to which camera is enabled/tagged as main. The batcher’s current `Camera.allCameras` diagnostic (`MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:320`, `MeshInstanceBatcher.cs:330`) is the right place to confirm the live split. This is the same class of failure as commit `6c7f4b4`: binding draw calls to a specific camera can silently render to the wrong view. The fix in `MeshInstanceBatcher.Flush()` is already to draw with `camera = null` instead of `CameraManager.MainCamera`, which removes that target-camera dependency.
docs\journeys\scratch\consolidated-audit-summary.md:20:6. Add `ProcGenCache` hit/miss counters and surface them in `RuntimeStatsOverlay` so cache regressions become visible instead of inferred (`procgen-cache-audit.md`).
docs\journeys\scratch\containerized-test-design.md:24:# DXVK and Steam stub are runtime overlays, not the game itself.
docs\journeys\scratch\cross-cutting-concerns.md:7:- Gap 1: logging is human-readable but not schema-driven. `BridgeServer` emits ad hoc strings and a JSON payload, while the stats overlay prints a fixed text line; neither carries stable fields like `event`, `component`, `request_id`, `setting_key`, or `duration_ms`. See [BridgeServer.cs](../../WorldSphereMod/Code/Bridge/BridgeServer.cs) and [RuntimeStatsOverlay.cs](../../WorldSphereMod/Code/Worldspace/RuntimeStatsOverlay.cs).
docs\journeys\scratch\cross-cutting-concerns.md:8:- Gap 2: telemetry stops at local console/UI and a pull endpoint. There is `/telemetry` plus the overlay, but no exporter, trace propagation, or alert hook for bridge failures, invalid requests, bundle load failures, or sustained perf regressions. `LocaleKeyCoverageTests` shows the repo already uses test-time verification for content invariants, but there is no runtime observability equivalent.
docs\journeys\scratch\cross-cutting-concerns.md:19:- Gap 1: there is no user-facing accessibility mode for color contrast. The UI and voxel paths use fixed colors and a single debug outline path; I did not find a color-blind palette, outline-contrast mode, or high-contrast theme toggle. See [WorldSphereTab.cs](../../WorldSphereMod/Code/WorldSphereTab.cs) and [RuntimeStatsOverlay.cs](../../WorldSphereMod/Code/Worldspace/RuntimeStatsOverlay.cs).
docs\journeys\scratch\cull-lift-final-verification.md:18:- `cullPos` is only used for visibility/lod selection.
docs\journeys\scratch\dead-code-candidates.md:7:  - symbols: GetSize, Bounds, AgeEffects, SetSize, CameraManager, MovementEnhancement, RotateCamera, GetSphereTileUnderMouse, Bounds3D, Size3D, MinZoomTranspiler, UpdateVelocity
